# p_graphop_s8: probe. Which operator inside an encoder layer holds the peak?
#
# basis      s8_encrypt_chunk's peak inside an encoder layer's forward:
#              run1   885,372 kB   585 ms before `layer|after_run_11`
#              run2   898,152 kB   688 ms before `layer|after_run_10`
#              run3   845,840 kB   717 ms before `layer|after_run_0`
#            bracketing markers 336,000 to 340,000 kB: ~545 MB transient in every layer (allocator decides
#            which sets the peak); 71.5% anon:residual.
# instrument graphop_markers_cpu: VmRSS and VmHWM after every graph node (VmHWM monotone: the jump node is
#            the cause). One /proc read + one stderr line per node; p_ prefix (off the line); output is a
#            location, not a peak. s8_encrypt_chunk's configuration.
# decides    one operator -> chunk it (as embed_chunk_cpu); spread over many -> line ends at 4.057x.
SHAFT_SCRIPT=$BASE/bert_perlayer_stream_cpu.py
SHAFT_LEVERS=graphop_markers_cpu,plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_chunk_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16 SHAFT_ENC_CHUNKS=8"
